{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/2493-dungeon-darkness","id":2493,"title":"Dungeon & Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-04T02:40:15-08:00","id":2493,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon12.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Dungeon & Darkness","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Darkness (English version 1.1)</b></span></div> <b>Introduction</b><br /> Hello, reader. Welcome to Dungeon &amp; Darkness<br /> If you are here, you really want to play Dungeons &amp; Dragons/Pathfinder as a theme, but you\u2019re probably not happy with the d20 System. Perhaps you always played World of Darkness and d20 System feels too combat heavy for you and not exactly that good for sandbox storytelling. Perhaps you feel like the World of Darkness is more realistic. Perhaps you feel like d20 System is just too complicated for your players and for yourself, and you do prefer a more easy and intuitive system. Or maybe you just want to try this game out for fun\u2019s sake.<br /> Whatever. I converted the d20 System to the Storyteller System because I really liked the idea and I felt I had the capability to do it. And I knew many people would have liked what I did. Thank you everyone for your support, have a nice campaign, adventure or read!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wait, this, this and this is referenced outside those books!!1!!!one!!!</b><br /> Everything that was not in these books was probably taken by the World of Darkness: Book of Spirits and Promethean: Pandora's Book. Mainly Numina. If you happen not to have those books, just ignore the Numina involved.<br /> I know that's a lot of book keeping to start with. But spells are referenced with the page number and they are likely the most part of the book keeping. You couldn't expect me to create all the spells from the start. <b>Contents</b><br /> <b>Chapter 1: Character creation </b>explains what you need to create your player character, with its race, class and the new mechanics.<br /> <b>Chapter 2: Magic and spells </b>defines what you need to know about magic, spells, magic items, special materials and the planes of existence.<br /> <b>Chapter 3: Monsters</b> is mainly aimed at Storytellers, with lots of examples of monsters, from dragons to devils and much more.<br /> <b>Appendix 1: Prestige classes</b> describes some of the prestige classes.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Appendix 2: Guidelines</span> for pre-GMC games describes how to play Dungeons &amp; Darkness without God-Machine Chronicles Rules Update.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Appendix 3: Conditions</span> lists new Conditions.<br /> <b>What you need to play?</b> You need a copy of the <b>World of Darkness corebook</b>, and the <b>God Machine Chronicle Rules Update</b>, available at DrivethruRPG.com for free, OR a copy of <b>God Machine Chronicle</b> though note that using the Appendix 2 you might ignore the book almost entirely except for ephemeral creatures rules.<br /> <b>Werewolf the Forsaken</b> and <b>Mage the Awakening</b> are also optional, but recommended. They might be useful to better understand the magic system and for reference for some spells.<br /> <b>Wait, this, this and this are referenced outside these books!</b><br /> Skill tricks are from <b>World of Darkness: Mirrors</b> (and aren't needed to enjoy the game), <b>World of Darkness: Book of Spirits</b> has some Numina that might be useful. Should you not have access to those books, you might buy them or ignore that specific rule entirely.<br /> <b>Theme: Magical Adventures</b> Dungeons &amp; Darkness is a game of adventure, great conflict, mysterious places, wonderful and intimidating creatures, and mystic items. A game where good and evil are a real thing. Behind every adventure there is a new mystery, a new story for the bards to tell, or a terrible secret to be buried under the ruins of an old dungeon. You might be adventuring for many reason. You might be in search of adventure to change your boring and grim life, to know yourself, to right the wrongs, to discover the world and grow knowledge, to witness many magical wonders, become rich and powerful, or even because you just got involved and cannot turn back anymore because it will cost you more than you\u2019re willing to give. It\u2019s a life of messy fights, discovery, intrigues, insidious and powerful magics, and cruel monsters. It\u2019s a game where deeds matter, and where you have to forge your own destiny through them.<br /> <b>Mood: Perpetual Conflict</b> The conflict between Good and Evil, between Law and Chaos, is everywhere. Powerful people have the capability to make their way of thought, to make their desires reality. The clash between powerful people creates conflict, that could be solved with a swift fight, or with a neverending war. Rival arcanists battle each other to determine who\u2019s the best. Political figures debate to rule their nations. Tyrants enforce the law oppressing the populations. Citizens struggle with the bossy and cruel dragons, who want to wrestle the control of cities, villages or even nations. Churches of the many faiths fight to establish their gods\u2019 will. Heaven makes war to the Hell.<br /> Where will you be when the conflict arises?<br /> Will you empower the conflict or will you end it?<br /> Is it even possible to cease all conflicts? Is it right?<br /> <br /> All rights to its rightful owners: Dungeons &amp; Darkness, World of Darkness, and everything else. No copyright infringment intended.<br /> <br /> <b>Dungeons &amp; Darkness 1.1 - Digital version, Work in progress</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit?pli=1</pre> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit?pli=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The pdf linked on google drive is outdated, and you should refer to the 1.1 version, but if you wish you can have a look at it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 09-01-2014, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T03:42:15-08:00","id":2498,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Arcanist</b><br /> <i>Hexblade Tradition</i><br /> <b>Class skills:</b> Occult, Subterfuge, Weaponry<br /> \u2022 Hex curse<br /> \u2022 \u2022 Aura of unluck 1/day<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Hexblade, Arcane restistance<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Aura of unluck 2/day<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Greater hex curse<br /> <b>Hex curse:</b> At 1st level, The hexblade can bestows a number of hex curse per day up to his Arcanist level. The character rolls Presence + Arete contested by Resolve + Arete of a target within 20 yards, and if the target fails it will recieve a -2 to all Attribute and Skill rolls for a scene or an hour, the shortest. Bestowing a hex curse is a Reflexive action during the hexblade's turn.<br /> <b>Aura of unluck:</b> At 2nd level once, at 4th twice, the hexblade can surround itself by an aura of unluck, forcing all attack against the hexblade to be rolled twice and take the worst result. This effect lasts 1 turn per hexblade level and can be activated as a Reflexive action during the hexblade's turn.<br /> <b>Hexblade:</b> At 3rd level and every level after, the character gains one dot in the Hexblade merit.<br /> <b>Arcane resistance:</b> At 3rd level the hexblade has +1 to contest all spells.<br /> <b>Greater hex curse:</b> At 5th level the penality of the hex curse becomes -3, and it will last all day.[/spoiler]<br /> <br /> <i>Spellthief Tradition</i><br /> <b>Class Skills:</b> Lacerny, Occult, Stealth<br /> \u2022 Sneak Attack 1, Steal spell (1) Trapfinding<br /> \u2022 \u2022 Arcane sight, Steal spell (2)<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Spellthief, Steal spell (3)<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Steal magical effects, Steal spell (4)<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Steal spell (5)<br /> <b>Trapfinding:</b> A spellthief gains the 9 Again rule when finding traps. The spellthief can also disable magical traps.<br /> <b>Sneak Attack:</b> At 1st level when the spellthief attacks an enemy unable to percieve him, unable to move, caught by surprise, or when attacked from two opposite sides the character adds +1 to the roll.<br /> <b>Steal spell:</b> When successfully using a sneak attack, the spellthief is immediately aware of all prepared or known spells of the target and can choose to steal a spell of first level and a spell per day. Within one hour from the theft, the spellthief can use that spell, casting it regularily. Meanwhile the spellcaster loses the access to that spell per day for a minute. The SLB for stolen spells is always +1. At every level thereafter, the spellthief can steal spells of one level higher.<br /> <b>Arcane sight:</b> At 2nd level, the spellthief has <i>detect magic</i> always on, but can choose to turn it off with a Reflexive action. The spellthief can reactivate it with an Istantaneous action. The Potency of the effect is 1.<br /> <b>Spellthief:</b> At 3rd level, and every level thereafter, the spellthief gains 1 dot in the Spellthief merit.<br /> <b>Steal magical effects:</b> At 4th level, the spellthief can steal one active magical effect instead of a spell, and the effect is transferred to the spellthief.<br /> <br /> <i>Warlock Tradition</i><br /> <b>Class Skills:</b> Occult, Intimidate, Persuasion<br /> \u2022 Detect magic, Eldritch blast, Warlock<br /> \u2022 \u2022 Fiendish resilience (bashing)<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Energy resistance<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Fiendish resilience (lethal)<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Imbue item<br /> <b>Detect magic:</b> At 1st level the warlock can roll Wits + Occult to cast <i>detect magic</i> as a spell-like ability, at will.<br /> <b>Eldritch blast:</b> The warlock can throw a blast of pure magical energy to cast as a ranged weapon. The warlock must roll Presence + Ranged. The damage is 1L, but becomes one point higher every level.<br /> <b>Warlock:</b> At 1st level and every level thereafter the warlock gains 1 dot in the Warlock merit.<br /> <b>Fiendish resilience (bashing):</b> At 2nd level, once per day the warlock can summon its dark powers to heal 1 bashing per Presence turns.<br /> <b>Energy resistance:</b> Select one element between acid, cold, electricity and fire. You suffer 1 damage less by that element.<br /> <b>Fiendish resilience (lethal):</b> At 3rd level, you can choose to heal 1 lethal instead of bashing with your Fiendish resilience.<br /> <b>Imbue item: </b>When creating a magic item, you don't need to cast the exact spell.<br /> <br /> <i>Warmage Tradition</i><br /> <b>Class Skills:</b> Intimidate, Occult, Warfare<br /> \u2022 Blast edge, Sudden Widen, Warmage<br /> \u2022 \u2022 Advanced learning<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Sudden Empower 1/vg<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Advanced learning<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Sudden Empower 2/vg<br /> <b>Blast edge:</b> When dealing damage with a spell, the warmage can inflict 1 extra bashing damage. A single spell cannot benefit more than once of the blast edge: ex. a <i>magic missile</i> thrown at more than one people is going to inflict 1 extra bashing only to one target. Same for things like <i>fireball</i> and other area spells.<br /> <b>Sudden Widen:</b> At first level, once per day, the warmage can use affect a spell like it had the Widen Spell merit for free, but only upgrading its Target or Area factor by one.<br /> <b>Warmage:</b> At 1st level and every level thereafter the warmage gains 1 dot in the Warmage merit.<br /> <b>Advanced learning:</b> At 2nd and 4th level, the warmage selects one sorcerer/wizard rote to add to his known spells. The spell must be of the Evokation school.<br /> <b>Sudden Empower:</b> Once per day at 3rd level, twice at 5th, the Warmage can benefit from the Empower Spell merit for free while casting a spell.<br /> <br /> <i>Wu Jen Tradition</i><br /> <b>Class Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Politics<br /> \u2022 Elemental mastery, Watchful Spirit, Wu Jen, Taboo<br /> \u2022 \u2022 Spell secret<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Spell secret<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Spell secret<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Spell secret<br /> <b>Elemental mastery:</b> At 1st level, Select one of the following elements: earth, fire, metal, water and wood. When casting spells belonging to this elements, you have +1 to the casting roll. At 5th level the bonus becomes +2.<br /> <b>Watchful spirit:</b> Once per day the wu jen can reroll the Initiative.<br /> <b>Wu jen:</b> At 1st level and every level thereafter the wu jen gains 1 dot in the Wu Jen merit.<br /> <b>Spell secret:</b> At 2nd level and every level thereafter the wu jen can select one of its known spell from the spellbook and treat it as always enhanced by one of the following Metamagic merits: Silent Spell, Still Spell (both without expending Willpower), Extended Spell or Widen Spell (only the first spellcasting factor).<br /> <b>Taboo:</b> To maintain their supernatural power, wu jen must abide by certain taboos that might seem inconsequential to other characters but are vitally important to the wu jen. If a wu jen violates one of her taboos, she cannot cast any more spells that day. A wu jen must choose one taboo per level. Sample taboos include &quot;cannot eat meat&quot;, &quot;Cannot own more than she can carry&quot; &quot;Must make daily offerings&quot; &quot;Cannot bathe&quot; &quot;Cannot cut her hair&quot;, &quot;Cannot touch a dead body&quot;, &quot;Cannot drink alcohol&quot;, &quot;Cannot wear a certain color&quot; &quot;Cannot light a fire&quot;, &quot;Cannot sit facing in a certain direction&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">Hexblade Rotes List https://docs.google.com/document/d/18fl9fisiMD1mJmxEvUwrsx7qxPeADAEq91K1hj4UCkY/edit</pre> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Hexblade (</b></span>\u2022<span style=\"color:#000000\"><b> to </b></span>\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> Your character can cast hexblade spells. At the first dot, the character obtains three first level rotes, from the hexblade rotes list. Follow the table below for the higher levels. He needs not to prepare them in advance, because all known rotes are automatically prepared, though an hexblade cannot learn new rotes with scrolls. To renew his daily spells he still needs 4 hours of rest. The character can cast a number of spells per day equal to the sum Occult and double his Arcanist level, plus 2. An hexblade can cast in armor if the mundane Armor value is not higher than 2.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Hexblade Spells Known</b></span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Merit dots</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">First level</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Second level</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Third level</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">1</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">3</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">4</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">3</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">5</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">3</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2</span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Spellthief (</b><b>\u2022</b><b> to </b><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><b>)<br /> Benefit:</b> Your character can cast spellthief spells. At the first dot, the character obtains three first level rotes, from the spellthief rotes list. Follow the table below for the higher levels. He needs not to prepare them in advance, because all known rotes are automatically prepared, though a spellthief cannot learn new rotes with scrolls. To renew his daily spells he still needs 4 hours of rest. The character can cast a number of spells per day equal to the sum Occult and double his Arcanist level, plus 2. An spellthief can cast in armor if the mundane Armor value is not higher than 2.<br /> <b>Spellthief Spells Known</b></span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Merit dots</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">First level</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Second level</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Third level</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">1</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">3</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">4</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">3</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">5</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">3</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2</span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Warmage (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Benefit: </b>The character can cast warmage spells. At first dot, the character knows all first level warmage rotes. Every new merit dots thereafter, he knows the next level list of warmage rotes. He needs not to prepare them in advance, because all known rotes are automatically prepared, though a warmage cannot learn new rotes with scrolls. To renew his daily spells he still needs 4 hours of rest. The character can cast a number of spells per day equal to the sum Occult and double his Priest level, plus 2.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Warlock (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Benefit:</b> The character can cast warlock invocations. At first dot, the character knows three warlock least invocations. Follow the table below for higher levels, gaining access to lesser, greater and dark invocations. At the fifth dot, the warlock can select two invocations of any level. He needs not to prepare them in advance, and can cast them at will. A warlock can cast invocations in armor if the mundane Armor value is not higher than 2.</span></span></span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Merit dots</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Least</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Lesser</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Greater</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dark</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">1</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">3</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">4</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">3</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">5</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">3</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">4</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">6</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">4</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">3</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">5</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Special</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Special</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Special</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Special</span></td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 12-19-2013, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T04:14:41-08:00","id":6730,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/1Gu2mPHt7YXRAlx6QNrid_nW1NAr0BCSFrMadlb_bbIFABgr8IC2HpwzzSDFf/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/1Gu2mPHt7YXRAlx6QNrid_nW1NAr0BCSFrMadlb_bbIFABgr8IC2HpwzzSDFf/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/file/d/1Gu2m...?usp=drive_web</a></a><br /> <br /> Hello people! For my birthday, my sister and my friends printed me this amazing book! The photos and illustrations are photos of me (cover and other pictures) and my friends of mine! There are some typos and formatting errors, but the file is mostly ok!<br /> <br /> Have a nice game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:59:09-08:00","id":11319,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>New Skill Tricks</b></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><b>Occult</b><br /> Except <b>Mental Healing</b>, all Occult Skill Tricks use tropes a bit out of place for D&amp;D<br /> <b>Arcane zoology (Story Advancement): </b>The characteris expert when dealing with misterious and magical creatures. When rolling Occult to understand a monster and its powers, double the Occult dots.<br /> <b>Magic Arts Defense (Extra talent): </b>The character knows a minor ritual that allows it to obtain a minor protection against magic, allowing him to resist against a spell. The ritual needs a calm place and 10 minutes. The character gains +2 to contest the next magical effect on him.<br /> <b>Magical Aptitude (Extra talent):</b>The character has innate magic power within himself. The character gains the ability to cast a first level rote as a spell-like ability (Wits + Occult) once per day. The spell can be any first level rote, regardless of the class it belongs.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Ride</b><br /> Ride is mostly like Drive. Two Skill Tricks still work for Ride: <b>Lose 'em,</b> <b>Shortcuts.</b><br /> <b>Expert Rider (Extra Talent): </b>When trying to put its mount under control (in case it was scared by combat or other things that usually scare mounts), the rider can add double its Ride dots for rolls.<br /> <b>Mounted rush (Combat): </b>The character is adept at using the mount as a weapon, making it run against opponents. When doing so, he moves the mount against an enemy, and rolls Dexterity + Ride. If it's successful, the rider rolls the successes or the mount's Size, whichever is higher, dealing bashing damage +2. If the mount crashes on an armored or really hard object or creature, it suffers 1 lethal damage and the rider takes -1 to all Ride rolls for the rest of the scene.<br /> <b>Ride by attack (Combat):</b> The character is expert at hit and run tactics while mounted. While doing so the mount and its rider move up to the Mount's Speed, and the rider can choose to attack one adjacent creature within the path of the mount with a Melee attack, at -2. Long weapons like spears, halberds, naginatas and quarterstaves do not suffer this penality.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Warfare</b><br /> <b>Battlefield Master (Extra Talent): </b>The character can ignore up to 2 points of penality to Warfare rolls caused by hazardous or difficult terrain.<br /> <b>Quick Skirmish (Time saver): </b>When confronted in quick battles against an army of lower Arete or Rank than the character, and having an army at his disposal the character can expend 1 Willpower point and roll Intelligence + Warfare against against the highest Intelligence and Warfare in the enemy group. The roll is penalized by the difference between the Size of the armies, whether to the attacker or to the defender, the character cannot use this Skill Trick. If the character wins, the leader of the roll must choose whether to take the Beaten Tilt or to deal an inconvenient to the character's army but otherwise be forced to run away safely.<br /> <b>Impending ambush</b> <b>(Penality):</b> The character is almost always alert for danger, the character gives Warfare as a penality to all Stealth rolls to ambush him or its allies.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 12-04-2013, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T11:38:00-08:00","id":14805,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Priest</b><br /> <i>Favored Soul Tradition</i><br /> Favored souls cast divine spells by means of an innate connection rather than through laborious training and prayer, so their divine connection is natural rather than learned.<br /> <b>Class Skills: </b>Academics, Empathy, Occult</span></span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Favored Soul</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 \u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Deity favored weapon</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 \u2022 \u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Energy resistance</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wings</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Divine resilience</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Favored Soul: </b>At 1<sup>st</sup> level and every level thereafter the favored soul gains 1 dot in the Favored Soul merit.<br /> <b>Deity favored weapon: </b>At 2<sup>nd</sup> level the character's gains a Specialization with the favored weapon of his deity, in the appropriate Skill.<br /> <b>Energy resistance: </b>Select one element between acid, cold, electricity and fire. You suffer 1 damage less by that element.<br /> <b>Wings: </b>At 4<sup>th</sup> level, the favored soul gets feathery or batlike wings, allowing it to fly at double its land Speed.<br /> <b>Divine resilience: </b>At 5<sup>th</sup> level, a lawful favored soul gains Armor 1 (except against attacks from chaotic outsiders and chaotic weapons), while a chaotic favored soul gains Armor 1 (except against attacks from lawful outsiders and lawful weapons). A neutral favored soul chooses either.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Shugenja Tradition</i><br /> The shugenja is a divine spellcaster who casts spells by attuning himself to the primal energies around him and focusing such energy through his body to produce magical effects.<br /> <b>Class Skills: </b>Academics, Investigate, Occult</span></span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Shugenja, Elemental focus, Percieve Element</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 \u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 \u2022 \u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elemental magic +1</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elemental magic +2</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Shugenja: </b>At 1<sup>st</sup> level and every level thereafter the shugenja gains 1 dot in the Shugenja merit.<br /> <b>Elemental focus:</b> At 1<sup>st</sup> level the character chooses one element between Air, Earth, Fire and Water. Opposed element spells (like Air vs Earth or Fire vs Water) are not available to Shugenja.<br /> <b>Percieve element:</b> Expending 1 Willpower point, the Shugenja can roll Investigation + Arete. One success reveals the presence, the Size and the location of one of the four elements, within 6 yards. Two successes reveal if the element is natural or a magical effect. Tre successes reveal if it's a creature or an object. Four successes reveal the exact nature of the object/creature (ex. If it's a fire genie or a fire elemental, if the object is gold or stone, if the air is safe or ill). Alternatively, the successes can be used to widen the area of the perception by 6 yards. Living creatures belong to all elements, and they can be revealed with any element.<br /> <b>Elemental magic:</b> At 3<sup>rd</sup> level, spells belonging to the elemental focus of the Shugenja have +1 (+2 at 5<sup>th</sup> level) to activation rolls.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Spirit Shaman Tradition</i><br /> By bargaining with living spirits, the spirit shaman gains power over the natural world and mighty divine magic.<br /> <b>Class skills: </b>Medicine,Occult<b>, </b>Survival.</span></span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Spirit shaman, Chastise spirits, Spirit sight</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 \u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ward against spirits</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 \u2022 \u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Spirit Form, Exorcism</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Recall spirit</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022</span></span></td> <td width=\"298\" class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Favored of the Spirits</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Spirit Shaman:</b> At 1<sup>st</sup> level and every level thereafter the spirit shaman gains 1 dot in the Spirit Shaman merit.<br /> <b>Chastise spirit:</b> At 1<sup>st</sup> level, the spirit shaman can damage hostile spirits with Wits + Spirit Shaman level, dealing 1 bashing per success to all spirits within 9 yards from the spirit shaman itself. A spirit shaman can chastise spirit only (Wits) times per day.<br /> <b>Detect spirits:</b> At 1<sup>st</sup> level, the character can roll Wits + Occult to Reflexively find creatures within sight for the rest of the scene, even in the Ethereal Plane. Any penality for anti-detection effects apply.<br /> <b>Ward against spirits: </b>At 2<sup>rd</sup> level, once per day, taking 10 minutes to practice the right ritual, the spirit shaman grants one creature per level the capability to affect spirits like they were manifested, and +1 to their Defenses and contested rolls.<br /> <b>Spirit form:</b> At 3<sup>rd</sup> level, once per day, the spirit shaman can turn incorporeal for up to 1 minute. While in spirit form, the spirit smana can damage both corporeal and incorporeal creatures, damaging with its touch (a 0B weapon). It also loses the Armor derived by physical means (like armor and thick skin)<br /> <b>Exorcist: </b>At 3<sup>rd</sup> level, a spirit shaman gains +2 to all abjure and exorcism rolls.<br /> <b>Recall Spirit:</b> At 4<sup>th</sup> level, once per day, a spirit shaman can resurrect a creature dead within one turn. Necromancy spells, a ruined corpse or any spell that seals away the soul of the target prevents this kind of resurrection.<br /> <b>Favored of the Spirits: </b>At 5<sup>th</sup> level, performing a rite that requires 8 hours, if a spirit shaman would be killed by an attack or spell, the attack or spell is instead nullified, and the protection from the rite discharges. Performing this rite is exhausting, and requires the expenditure of a Willpower <i>dot.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">edit:</span> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>What is a spirit?</b><br /> All incorporeal undead, all fey, all elementals, creatures in astral body, aligned outsiders (angels, archons, devils, demons and the like). Elementals and fey are called spirits of nature, ghosts are called as spirits of the dead.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">Shugenja Rotes List https://docs.google.com/document/d/10bbVxsfowJjbwnp5rbKTbFcs_bDwpMT9jKTJCk55wQ0/edit</pre> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Favored Soul (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Benefit:</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> The character can cast favored soul spells. At the first dot, the character obtains three first level rotes, from the cleric rotes list. Follow the table below for the higher levels. He needs not to prepare them in advance, because all known rotes are automatically prepared, though a favored soul cannot learn new rotes with scrolls. To renew his daily spells he still needs 4 hours of rest. The character can cast a number of spells per day equal to the sum Occult and double his Priest level, plus 2.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Favored Soul Spell known</b></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Merit dots</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">First level</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Second level</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Third level</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Fourth level</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Fifth level</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">1</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">4</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">5</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">4</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">6</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">4</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">5</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">7</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">5</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">4</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">2</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Spirit Shaman (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Benefit:</b> The character can cast spirit shaman spells. At first dot, the character knows all first level druid rotes. Every new merit dots thereafter, he knows the next level list of druid rotes. Before casting spells, the spirit shaman must prepare them. To prepare his spells, he needs four hours of rest, and than spend 15 minutes to become one with nature, meditating on the natural forces. The character can prepare a numer of spells up to Occult and its Priest level. The character can cast a number of spells per day equal to the sum of Occult and two times its Priest level.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Shugenja (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Benefit:</b> The character can cast shugenja spells. At the first dot, the character obtains three first level rotes, from the shugenja rotes list. Follow the table below for the higher levels. He needs not to prepare them in advance, because all known rotes are automatically prepared, though a shugenja cannot learn new rotes with scrolls. To renew his daily spells he still needs 4 hours of rest. The character can cast a number of spells per day equal to the sum Occult and double his Priest level, plus 2.</span></span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Merit dots</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">First level</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Second level</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Third level</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Fourth level</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Fifth level</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">1</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">4</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">5</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">4</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">6</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">4</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">-</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">5</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">7</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">5</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">4</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">2</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 12-19-2013, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:34:27-08:00","id":17026,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>NEW CONDITIONS</b></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Controller</b><br /> The character has gained insight when using mind-affecting magic. When using enchantment spells, the Duration is enhanced by one Duration Factor like with the Extended Spell merit, without penality.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>The character uses the benefit.<br /> <b>B</b><b>eat: </b>N/A</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Frayer</b><br /> The character has gained insight when using magic to damage. When using a spell that deals energy damage (fire \u2013 cold \u2013 electricity \u2013 acid), all target suffer 1 more bashing damage.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: The character uses the benefit.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>N/A<br /> <br /> <b>Spellslinger</b><br /> The character has gained insight when casting magic. If the character fails to cast a spell, the character can decide to use this Condition to do gain at least 1 success. If the roll was a chance die, the caster gains a single die instead.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> The mastery of the character guides him, the worst is gone. The Condition is resolved as above.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> N/A</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Seer</b><br /> The character has gained insight when using divination magic. When using spells like <i>divination</i>, <i>augury</i> and similar spells, the character can ask one more question.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>The character uses the benefit.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>N/A<br /> <br /> <b>Veil Master</b><br /> The character has gained insight when using illusion magic. When using illusions, they are counted as Potency +1 when they are to be detected with unveiling magic.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>The character uses the benefit.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>N/A</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Spell havoc</b><br /> The character's magical control is having problem in balancing magical energies, messing with its spells. The spell is no longer under the caster's control. It affects a randomly chosen target (or targets if multiple were factored into the casting) instead of the caster\u2019s declared target(s). The caster himself is a potential random victim. The new target must be of the same type (person, object, location, etc.). For example, if the caster targeted a person, then the pool of random targets includes only people. If the caster is the only viable target present, then he is the target of his own spell unless he was its originally intended target, in which case the spell affects a target of a different kind, such as an object. The new target \u2014 including the mage himself, if he is the spell\u2019s new target \u2014 can contest or resist the spell if it is normally allowed. In addition, the caster must roll Resolve + Composure. Every spell casted while in this Condition, applies -1 to this roll.With a success, the spell effect is unaltered. With a failure the desired effect is somehow reversed.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>The character must take some time to meditate (Target number 3) to rebalance its psyche or take an Exceptional Success at the Resolve + Composure roll.<br /> <b>Beat</b>: When a really important casted spell is reversed because of the Resolve + Composure roll.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T23:48:59-08:00","id":18982,"title":"","content":"Well I asked this on the old forum but since it's just days away from being deleted I guess I'd better ask it here: How do you think these adventurers would fare sharing a world with the official WW splats?<br /> <br /> Because in the dnd setting of &quot;world of prime&quot; has a rational that I feel would make sense in nwod. Namely that adventurers collect the remnants of soul energy left behind by the dead, and consume this soul energy to craft their souls into forms that allow them the extranormal abilities all the adventurers have. <br /> <br /> Oh and any classes you aren't planning on including? I'd like to see your take on the ghost class for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T01:11:23-08:00","id":19026,"title":"","content":"Non-spellcasting classes (fighter, rogue and monk) are just mostly &quot;extraordinary mortals&quot; as power level. Though magic items can greatly improve their effectiveness and power, and the right magic items can make those classes really powerful. That's because in World of Darkness lots of damage is more likely to kill your opponent than in D&amp;D. Plus, if you can fly, teleport, become invisibile and things like that, you can beat a lot of enemies.<br /> <br /> You're either a really powerful hunter or a little less powerful mage.<br /> <br /> At the moment I don't plan to convert the Complete Warrior Samurai. Probably using the Pathfinder RPG Samurai. I don't know what to choose between the 3.5 Knight and the Pathfinder Knight. I also don't know how to bring the Eberron Artificer to life at the moment.<br /> I plan on converting the noble and the mystic from Dragonlance. I'm definitely going to include the classes from Advanced Player's Guide, Ultimate Magic, Ultimate Combat and perhaps, when it comes out, Advanced Class Guide. I also plan to include the new psionic classes from Ultimate Psionics.<br /> <br /> What do you mean by the ghost class? The only ghost classes I know are from Ghostwalk. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghostwalk\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghostwalk</a><br /> You mean something already existing?<br /> You mean how would I create a class on ghosts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T12:56:03-08:00","id":21258,"title":"","content":"I need your help people. I'm revising and tweaking (oh gosh all the typos and errors) D&amp;Darkness.<br /> As is, Integrity and Alignment doesn't feel quite right. I need to find a solution. At the moment the rules for alignment and Integrity are:<ul><li>Integrity GMC</li> <li>Integrity 7-10 (Good)</li> <li>Integrity 7-5 (Neutral)</li> <li>Integrity 1-4 (Evil)</li> <li>And add Law and Chaos tags. Low integrity characters can abjure and exorcise good creatures.</li> </ul><br /> But that's not working as intended. Alignment has little to do with insanity and Integrity. Yet I'm not sure how removing Integrity will affect the game.<br /> I need to find something that's more in theme with the game and something that actually works.<br /> <br /> EDIT: One of the worst things is that Breaking Points shouldn't lead you to become more evil. Remember in D&amp;D Good and Evil are more of a tangible force.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT 2:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think alignment is more like Virtue and Vice.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said this in the other thread (is there a way they can be merged? Cause this is a bit weird) but it bears repeating. I think getting rid of the 9-alignment system altogether is a huge pro of converting to the storytelling system. If you want to model alignment on the two axies of Good/Evil and Law/Chaos though, I would probably use the Morality stat as your sliding scale of Good vs. Evil and your Powerstat as a sliding scale of Law vs. Chaos. Unfortunately you've already god Arete as your powerstat, so I'm not sure what else you should do.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>@Charlaquin:</b> I didn't want to dirty the original thread too much, but perhaps you're right. Sorry for the inconvinience.<br /> Not so sure about that. Many people playing D&amp;D still like the feel of the nine alingments. Good and Evil, Law and Chaos are tangible forces in D&amp;D.<br /> A Banisher mage isn't necessarily evil. A Banisher is capable of doing &quot;good&quot; things. The banisher could kill those evil Guardians of the Veil who killed that family of Sleepers who accidentally came to know too much about Supernal magic<br /> A cleric of Lolth or Erythnul...no. Lolth is a goddess of opportunism. If you are weak, you should die. A cleric of Erythnul feels emotions for sure. But not compassion, more probably enthusiastic hate and bloodlust.<br /> Plus, paladins are going to be problematic to arrange. Paladins are all about alignment. Removing alignments means taking away and twisting much of their flavour and class features. And it would require me to create other 3 classes from scratch (tiranny, destruction and freedom).<br /> <br /> <b>@Rose Bailey</b>: That would be something I would consider. Though on the contrary of Virtues and Vices, Alignments are not that freeform.<br /> I was also considering using Alignments to regain Willpower, but the Neutral part would be problematic to define. What is &quot;acting neutral&quot;? Is &quot;being actively neutral&quot; even a plausible thing?<br /> EDIT: Quoting your posts in the original thread. This thread can be closed.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 12-01-2013, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T13:46:47-08:00","id":21271,"title":"","content":"Emphasis mine<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/2493-dungeon-darkness?p=21258#post21258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need your help people. I'm revising and tweaking (oh gosh all the typos and errors) D&amp;Darkness.<br /> As is, Integrity and Alignment doesn't feel quite right. I need to find a solution. At the moment the rules for alignment and Integrity are:<ul><li>Integrity GMC</li> <li>Integrity 7-10 (<b>Lawful</b>)</li> <li>Integrity 7-5 (<b>Neutral</b>)</li> <li>Integrity 1-4 (<b>Chaotic</b>)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I think integrity more closely reflects the insanity of the Law and Chaos axis than it does the Good and Evil Axis.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though I like Rose's suggestion, I think Charlaquin is closer to what will actually work. Make TWO integrity scales for the characters, one being the Lawful-Chaotic scale and the other being the Good-Evil scale, and then construct special conditions for each. When building the conditions, though, do not think of them as detriments, rather think of them as personality components that are made more prevalent as the character drifts on the alignment scale.<br /> <br /> That is, perhaps rising on the Good-Evil scale with a particularly high success imposes a 'good' condition that influences certain behaviors, and falling on the Law-Chaos scale with a particularly heavy failure imposes a 'chaos' condition that likewise influences certain behaviors.<br /> <br /> ...I sort of lost the wind from my sails at the end there. But you follow my intention, yes?<br /> <br /> EDIT: As for breaking points making you more evil, that's a matter of properly defining breaking points on the Good-Evil scale. There ARE actions that result in a change in alignment... such actions are what you should consider 'breaking points' in this model.<br /> <br /> EDIT EDIT: It might work better if you apply the breaking point model in both directions. There would be 'good' breaking points that raise the scale, and 'evil' breaking points that lower it. You can even make the dots do double duty: against evil-aligned magic a character uses the empty dots for supernatural resistance, against good-aligned magic a character uses the filled dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":". 12-01-2013, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T15:28:27-08:00","id":21322,"title":"","content":"Without getting too far off topic, I would like to respond to what you mentioned in the other thread. I think you misunderstood my issue with alignment. Good/Evil, Law/Chaos as tangible things, and characters being rated on where they fall on both scaled is an important part of D&amp;D's identity, I agree. My problem is with the nine neat little boxes everyone is expected to fall into. That's why I didn't recommend they replace Virtue and Vice, even though they are the most obvious parallel in the storytelling system. Rather, i think it is very important that both axies be measured, but on a sliding scale rather than a simple positive/neutral/negative for each. Thinking on it, I agree with the suggestion of having two Morality stats, one for Good/Evil and one for Law/Chaos. Additionally, since D&amp;D has a long tradition of alignment shifting based on the character's actions, all you need to do is have &quot;breaking points&quot; that apply in either direction. So killing innocent people will drive you towards Evil, while selfless acts will drive you towards Good. Upholding and enforcing law and order will push you towards Lawful, and breaking laws or disrupting established governing systems will push you towards Chaos. Neutrality can be maintained either by keeping a balance, or simply not getting involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T00:55:57-08:00","id":23003,"title":"","content":"Yes, I meant the ghost class from ghostwalk. While I found the setting rather humanocentric in its metaphysics, I quite liked the premise. <br /> <br /> Perhaps one could come up with breaking points for chaos, good, evil, and order? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T09:44:16-08:00","id":23199,"title":"","content":"<b>Eidolon (Prestige class)<br /> Tier 1: </b>Rank 1 ghost, must have had at least Arete 1 while alive, Resolve 2.<br /> <b>Phantom Arete: </b>The eidolon uses its Rank instead of Arete to gain class levels, regaining all class levels it had in life.<br /> <b>Influences and Numina: </b>The eidolon retains all of its Influences and Numina. The character uses Presence + Resolve to uses Influences, and Resolve + Occult to use Numina.<br /> <b>Wraith:</b> The eidolon uses the flesh rules for Attributes, Skills and Merits even while incorporeal.<br /> <b>Tier 2: </b>Rank 3 ghost<br /> <b>Influences and Numina: </b>The eidolon gains bonus 1 Numina.<br /> <b>Tier 3: </b>Rank 5 ghost<br /> <b>Numina:</b> The eidolon gains bonus 1 Numina.<br /> <br /> I treated as a prestige class, while I know there are some prestige classes in the Ghostwalk for ghosts, I didn't want to go that deep, as it is an indeed niche part of D&amp;D.<br /> In any case, both Eidolon and Eidoloncer are done this way. Any class can take this prestige class, and still gain spells, numina and things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T14:30:02-08:00","id":23316,"title":"","content":"New Occult Skill tricks up at post #4 ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T13:24:03-08:00","id":25316,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Alignment Breaking points</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Good towards Evil</span></b></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Character is protecting a loved one or an innocent</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">+2</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Character is acting in accordance with its Virtue</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">+1</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Character is acting in accordance with its Vice</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-1</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Harming a good creature</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-3 to -5</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Torture</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-3</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Using evil magic/Bringing Evil into the Material Plane (creating undead, summoning fiends)</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-4</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Evil towards Good</b></span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Character is feigning goodness</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">+2</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Character is acting in accordance with its Virtue</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">+1</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Character is acting in accordance with its Vice</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-1</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Righting wrongs you did to others</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-2</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Really selfless actions</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-3 to -5</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Using good magic/Bringing Good into the Material Plane (summoning celestials)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-4</span></td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Law towards Chaos</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Betray your nation, family, friend or partner</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-2 to -5</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Breaking a meaningful promise</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-1 to -3</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Character is acting in accordance with its Virtue</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">+1</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Character is acting in accordance with its Vice</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-1</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Major crime (vandalism, black market, murder etc.)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-3 to -5</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Minor crime (non violent, low-money, victimless)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-1 or -2</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Fighting an unjust law or norm</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">+2</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Using chaotic magic/Bring Chaos into the Material Plane (summoning chaotic creatures)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-4</span></td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Chaos towards Law</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Betraying or surrender your individuality when meaningful</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-1 to -3</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Character is acting to protect his or another's free will</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">+2</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Character is acting in accordance to its Virtue</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-1</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Character is acting in accordance to its Vice</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">+1</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Rejecting a good change</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-1 to -4</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Using lawful magic/Bringing Law into the Material Plane (summoning lawful creatures)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-4</span></td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The character\u2019s world view has been changed drastically. The character suffers from traumatic stress. Shift one dot in the appropriate Axis and choose from the following Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller approval): Broken, Fugue, Guilty. Also, take a Beat.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The character\u2019s world view has been shaken and he probably questions his sense of self, his ability to relate to people, his own moral worth. Shift one dot in the appropriate Axis and choose one of the following Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller approval): Guilty, Shaken, Obsession.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The character has come through the breaking point intact. He might feel guilty or upset about what happened, but he can cope. Choose one of the following Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller approval): Guilty, Shaken, Steadfast.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The character somehow manages not only to survive the breaking point, but to find meaning in it, to reaffirm his own self-worth, or to pass through fire and become tempered by it. The character takes a Beat and regains a point of Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 12-09-2013, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T03:21:32-08:00","id":28610,"title":"","content":"Any opinion? Good, bad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T04:58:02-08:00","id":28637,"title":"","content":"Actually, one of the DMs with which I played used a similar system for our D&amp;D games. It worked very well, especially when we played in the Dragonlance setting and he needed to decided which robes I'll wear (black robs, of course :P)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T20:27:18-08:00","id":30242,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks for the prestige class, although I'd have reversed a few things, since the gmc won't let you become past rank 2 losing all your anchors and going to the underworld essentially forever the players won't be encountering a ghost with effective arete of 3 or more without dungeon diving in the underworld. Well unless you meant for ghosts to be able to still buy more arete even while dead, or have a system for creatures gaining rank that I missed.<br /> <br /> I was wondering, have you playtested this? I just can't help how a few things play out when it actually get's played.<br /> <br /> In dnd class is everything, but since attributes and skills are unrelated to further arete purchases I'm not sure how much the non spellcasting classes will care about gaining arete. If you want an even closer emulation of dnd you might want to include an option that arete adds to health levels and attack rolls, using that option from mirrors. <br /> <br /> I also wonder about balance with the spellcasting classes, have you found that the exp payments for their spellcasting merits and arete prevent spellcasters from basically going codzilla like magic knights? <br /> <br /> Do you have bleeding edge the cyberpunk book? It has party niche merits, for like the street samarai, the hacker, etc, which is a concept I thought you might want to adapt for this project, perhaps tie it to class level, perhaps not, it would help elevate adventurers so that a rogue will be better than a &quot;commoner&quot; with some dots in larceny, etc. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, my computer just died so I can't be more specific with how those merits work in bleeding edge. Does anyone else with that book think that makes sense? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T00:42:50-08:00","id":30319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cool, thanks for the prestige class, although I'd have reversed a few things, since the gmc won't let you become past rank 2 losing all your anchors and going to the underworld essentially forever the players won't be encountering a ghost with effective arete of 3 or more without dungeon diving in the underworld. Well unless you meant for ghosts to be able to still buy more arete even while dead, or have a system for creatures gaining rank that I missed. </div> </div> </div>No you don't improve your Arete, you use Rank instead of Arete. You gain Rank the same way you gain Arete (Experience...). You could disregard entirely the need of an Eidolon to stay much time in the Underworld or near the Anchor, if that works best for you.<br /> I haven't playtested <b>this prestige class</b> yet. As for the <b>game</b> itself, yes, I've converted a Pathfinder game to this. The game is playing smoothier than Pathfinder or D&amp;D. Though it still has its rule holes and some errors from the book. And spellcasting pool is perhaps a little too high if you start at an experienced level instead of starting from level 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In dnd class is everything, but since attributes and skills are unrelated to further arete purchases I'm not sure how much the non spellcasting classes will care about gaining arete. If you want an even closer emulation of dnd you might want to include an option that arete adds to health levels and attack rolls, using that option from mirrors. </div> </div> </div>Actually, the game already has. There is an optional hack in the book, called <b>System hack: High level hit points</b> that adds health levels. I use it. Know that while non spellcasting classes don't gain spells, they still gain <b>class features</b>, AND <b>health</b> (with the hack) AND <b>resistance to supernatural effects</b>, AND more importantly, the possibility to use <b>2 Willpower per turn</b>!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also wonder about balance with the spellcasting classes, have you found that the exp payments for their spellcasting merits and arete prevent spellcasters from basically going codzilla like magic knights? </div> </div> </div>Spellcasting merits are not payed for. They're granted by leveling in the appropriate class. Wizard only pay new rotes added from scrolls and other spellbooks.<br /> .<br /> As for codzillas, I nerfed the stat boosting spells, and I was careful not to create too many &quot;+1 to this and to that&quot; spells. What you might see is that a wizard might take high Melee, high Strenght and Stamina and &quot;go melee&quot;. That's fine. The &quot;meleer&quot; classes are still going to have many class features you will be losing and won't be able to obtain if not by taking &quot;meleer&quot; class levels. You can't prepare too many spells at time like you could in D&amp;D, so you'll better choose your spells wisely. Same for clerics. Focusing on buffing up when you should maybe prepare a dispel magic and more &quot;wizardey&quot; spells, will be a problem.<br /> Then, use magic device also doesn't exist anymore the same way it did. A &quot;fighter&quot; or &quot;rogue&quot; could take a wand, roll the wand level + Occult to activate the wand itself.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm looking forward to give spellcasters a nerf. Concentration at the moment doesn't exist. I'm going to create penalities for spellcasting while in melee.<br /> <br /> As for Bleeding edge, I'll be looking at it to better answer you, as for now I'm in a hurry. Have a good day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 12-15-2013, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T01:01:45-08:00","id":30324,"title":"","content":"I got a swift look to the merits. I think they would work just fine, though you might need to adapt it here and there to the context of your game. Consider though Role would probably be overlapping a little too much with Professional Training in GMC and Hunter the Vigil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T06:20:43-08:00","id":30393,"title":"","content":"<b>Oreste<br /> Quote: </b>&quot;<i>Leave me be or soon your soul will leave your body!</i>&quot;<br /> <b>Concept:</b>Wanted monk criminal<br /> <b>Class: </b>Monk 1\u00b0 <b>Race: </b>Human<br /> <b>Alignment:</b> Chaotic Evil <b>Virtue: </b>Patient<b> Vice: </b>Greedy<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Intelligence 2 Wits 2 Resolve 3 Strenght 2 Dexterity 4 Stamina 2 Presence 2 Manipulation 2 Composure 2<br /> <b>Skills: </b>Academics 1 Investigation 2 Occult 2, Athletics 3, Brawl (kathar) 3 Ranged 2 Stealth 3, Animal ken 1 Intimidate 3 Subterfuge 4<br /> <b>Merit:</b> Fighting Style Martial Arts 3, Magic Item (Katar +1) 1, Fighting Finesse, Professional Training (&quot;Thug&quot;, Brawl, Intimidation) 2, Resources 1.<br /> <b>Skill Trick: </b>Fastest of them All (Time saver)<br /> <b>Health: </b>7<b> Defense:</b> 7 <b>Willpower</b>: 5 <b>Iniz:</b> 6 (5 with kathar or knife) <b>Size:</b> 5 <b>Speed</b>:11<br /> <b>Attack:</b><br /> Katar +1, 2L, 8 dice, 9 again, Brawl based.<br /> Knife, throwing 1L, 7 dice<br /> <br /> <b>Blackmoon<br /> Quote: </b>&quot;<i>I won't let you leave, you're not going to be a problem to my city any longer!</i>&quot;<br /> <b>Concept:</b> Fighter mage at the city guard's service.<br /> <b>Class: </b>Wizard 1\u00b0 <b>Race: </b>Human<br /> <b>Alignment: </b>Lawful neutral <b>Virtue:</b> Just <b>Vice: </b>Hasty<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Intelligence 3 Wits 2 Resolve 2 Strenght 3 Dexterity 2 Stamina 3 Presence 2 Manipulation 2 Composure 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3 Occult 3 Investigation 2, Athletics 3 Melee (sword) 3 Ranged 2 Stealth 3, Persuasion 3, Socialize 1<br /> <b>Merit:</b> Allies (city guard) 1, Area of Expertize (Sword), Extended Spell 2, Professional Training (&quot;Soldier&quot;,Athletics and Melee) 2, Resources 2, Silent Spell, Wizard 1.<br /> <b>Skill trick:</b> Always investigating (Extra Talent)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8 <b>Defense:</b> 5 <b>Willpower:</b> 4 <b>Initiative:</b> 4 (2 with Sword)<br /> <b>Spells:</b> 1<sup>st</sup> level: Magic missile, Magic Weapon, Shocking grasp. 5 per day.<br /> <b>Spellbook:</b> 1<sup>st</sup> level: Magic missile, Magic weapon, Shocking grasp.<br /> <b>Attack:</b><br /> Sword 2L, 7 dice, 9 again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oreste just killed a couple of guards, who couldn't even scratch the monk because of its speed. Blackmoon was trying to catch Oreste running him over, but he manged to escape thanks to his superior speed (Fastest of them All skill trick). She thinks he's hidden in a granary. She has all motivation to bring Oreste to justice or to kill him.<br /> Her inability to catch him costed her many sacrifices, including her status within the city guards. But she's prepared now. She casts <i>magic weapon</i> on her sword to make it a 3L.<br /> Blackmoon enters the granary, hoping to find Oreste and defeat him for good.<br /> Oreste is hidden behind some sacks, eager to kill his nemesis, He rolls Dexterity 4 + Stealth 3 to hide, getting two successes. Blackmoon is well aware of Oreste's tricks, and watches out for peril. She rolls Wits 2 + Composure 2 + Investigate 2 (thanks to her Skill Trick), but only gets one success. Oreste is silent and sneaky, but as soon as Blackmoon appears inside the granary, he ambushes her with his katar, denying her the Defense.<br /> Luckily for her, Oreste misses, even with 8 dices. Time to roll for Initiative.<br /> Oreste's Initiative is a 7, Blackmoon's 3. Oreste is angry for the miss from the first time and decides to use one Willpower to get 3 extra dice for his next attack. Blackmoon's Defense is 5. And still no successes, even with 6 dice.<br /> Blackmoon's turn now. She starts with a full force swing against Oreste, to get +2 forgoing Defense. She also spends 1 Willpower to get 3 more dices. That's about 5 dices because of Oreste's Defense, a 7. First blood! With one success, Blackmoon scores 4 points of lethal damage with her sword.<br /> It's Oreste's chance to take out Blackmoon in one hit once again, and he chooses to forgo Defense and spend another Willpower Point to hit Blackmoon. She's vulnerabile now. 5 successes! Blackmoon is now 6L of 7 Health points! He also takes the Steadfast Condition.<br /> Blackmoon is really hurt, almost dead, and Stunned. She can spend her last Willpower Point to act but take -3 to all action she takes. She swings again, against no Defense, but at -3 and cannot spend Willpower. That's 4 dice, 9 again.With 1 success, Oreste is down to full lethal damage. If she wasn't Stunned, she could have casted Shocking Grasp and electrocuted Oreste.<br /> The monk crumbles to earth, along with Blackmoon<br /> <br /> A test for martial/caster disparity. Blackmoon didn't manage to use magic in a really meaningful way, and almost died. If instead of Fastest of them All Oreste had Size Up, he could have rerolled his first attack and probably dropped her dead really fast. Blackmoon only magic was <i>magic weapon</i> (which actually helped her a lot with damage output). She could have tried to beat Oreste a bit and then cast magic missile into full lethal damage, but Oreste would have fled outside of sight, allowing him to break line of sight.<br /> <br /> Not much to say here for now. First level is harsh for wouldbe fighter mages. I'll be playtesting higher level martial-caster disparity, i hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T15:05:20-08:00","id":30608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/2493-dungeon-darkness?p=25316#post25316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The character\u2019s world view has been changed drastically. The character suffers from traumatic stress. Shift one dot in the appropriate Axis and choose from the following Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller approval): Broken, Fugue, Guilty. Also, take a Beat.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The character\u2019s world view has been shaken and he probably questions his sense of self, his ability to relate to people, his own moral worth. Shift one dot in the appropriate Axis and choose one of the following Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller approval): Guilty, Shaken, Obsession.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The character has come through the breaking point intact. He might feel guilty or upset about what happened, but he can cope. Choose one of the following Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller approval): Guilty, Shaken, Steadfast.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The character somehow manages not only to survive the breaking point, but to find meaning in it, to reaffirm his own self-worth, or to pass through fire and become tempered by it. The character takes a Beat and regains a point of Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like everything in your alignment grid except for this. Specifically, I don't like that breaking points from different axes use the same list of conditions. I know it might be more to track, but perhaps constructing LAW, CHAOS, GOOD, and EVIL conditions would give the impact of a breaking point more potency.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here are a few examples I whipped up on the spot, they may or may not be functional<br /> <br /> Compulsive Truth (Law) -- Severe<br /> Your persistence in upholding law has suffused you with the uncontrollable urge to tell the truth, repeatedly and constantly. You are driven to interject meaningless details into every conversation, even when doing so would be embarrassing or dangerous.<br /> This condition is resolved when the character encounters another Law or Chaos breaking point. This condition gives beats when the compulsive truth places the character in a dangerous situation<br /> <br /> Compulsive Lies (Chaos) -- Severe<br /> Ditto, but for impulse mistruth. You are driven to altar facts whenever you speak, even when such lies would be immediately disproved and damage your credibility.<br /> <br /> Meadow Convergence (Good) -- Severe<br /> Whenever you are out in nature, friendly woodland creatures gather around you for no adequately explored reason.<br /> This condition is resolved the next time the character encounters an EVIL breaking point, or if she kills one of the woodland creatures<br /> <br /> Storm Clouds (Evil) -- Severe<br /> Whenever you speak, the weather seems to react in a dramatic and unexpected manner. Cracks of thunder, gathering storm-clouds, that sort of thing.<br /> This condition is resolved if the character becomes aware of the phenomenon and calls attention to it.<br /> <br /> Scratchy Throat (Chaos, Evil) -- Mild<br /> You have a cold. Or at least it sounds like you swallowed a frog (whether or not you actually did isn't important). This condition resolves after a few days.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...I know, the examples are cheesy (I was trying to be funny), but you get the idea, yeah?<br /> Then again, if you've already started using the system and the prefabricated conditions are working, feel free to ignore my warbles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I just want to take the opportunity to say how awesome everything you're doing here is. Keep up the great work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T15:51:54-08:00","id":30630,"title":"","content":"Thank you CJC for your support and suggestion. I too was trying to come up with something like that, but ultimately ended up with the conclusion that without external help I can only think on common ground Conditions, because that was too much work. And I was more concerned with breaking point grids.<br /> <br /> Actually, you just gave me an idea. Oh yeah. Exalted's going to help me out here. Some Virtue Flaws might be helpful to create alignment Conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T20:07:14-08:00","id":30713,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I guess it didn't occur to me that in this game the splats can count as professions, I imagine that most STs would laugh if a player tried to take professional: vampire after all. lol, I <br /> <br /> And I did notice the option to add arete to health, I was suggesting that some people might like the idea of it adding to attack rolls as well ala &quot;tough people, tough shots.&quot; Probably most people wouldn't, but in dnd a first level commoner is just ass to be mowed by a tenth level fighter if it comes to that, so I thought some people might like the idea as an option.<br /> <br /> Since my computer died and so my virtual copies of gmc and bleeding edge are unavailable to me at the moment I can't contrast and compare the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T00:29:08-08:00","id":30808,"title":"","content":"Well, it's not only about commoners, it's also about the 3.5 &quot;experts&quot; and &quot;warriors&quot;, who while not particularily powerful, they could still get high strenght and melee and do bad things. And they still can't get Skill Tricks. I don't know if you've seen Skill Tricks. Aaand Melee/Brawl/Whatever Skill Tricks are really powerful. A Fighter with the right Skill Trick is going mince their meats and make them cry like babies.<br /> I mean, experts and warriors can still be somewhat challenging at firsts levels, and should be.<br /> <br /> Ex: The same way vampires find humans scary. A neonate vampire is powerful, yes, but a dedicated combatant human is NOT THAT FAR away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 12-16-2013, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T22:05:15-08:00","id":31472,"title":"","content":"Well anyway I'm looking forward to you rounding out your list with a few more of the more exotic classes like artificers, dread warlocks, shadowcrafter, binder, etc.<br /> <br /> Are you planning on including some of the more unusual pc races like thri-keen, warforged, shifter, or dragonborn later? Speaking of unusual races, I'm certainly not holding my breath waiting for you to do all the savage species classes, because that would what, triple your workload there, but I am curious if there were any monster classes you ever converted or considered converting. <br /> <br /> Or perhaps that's just because I've gotten into radiance d20, since it has classes which are about being more like a vampire, werewolf, or dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T00:22:28-08:00","id":31525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well anyway I'm looking forward to you rounding out your list with a few more of the more exotic classes like artificers, dread warlocks, shadowcrafter, binder, etc. </div> </div> </div>Of course. Though probably the Tome of Magic ones will be somewhat the most difficult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you planning on including some of the more unusual pc races like thri-keen, warforged, shifter, or dragonborn later? </div> </div> </div>I'm not planning to, but they're quite easy to convert. I'll do my try for those races too if you wish.<br /> I don't need to make any Savage Species book. Most races can be converted with ease. Hit dice is not necessarily a thing, as races that are more powerful, simply are more powerful. You're not going to expect a Troll or a Fire Giant to be on par with a human. As for some monsters...well:<br /> <br /> Ex: You want to be a succubus bard? You are a 3rd level character. You want to be a Rank 1 earth elemental fighter 1\u00b0? You're a second level. You want to be lower level? Take away some points of natural armor and lower your Rank (that means also Influences Numina and Manifestations are lower). As for the succubus, you might want to use flesh rules for her Attributes and Skills, because spirit Attributes can become quite powerful OR quite shitty.<br /> <br /> OF COURSE they're not necessarily going to be balanced for play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T05:07:54-08:00","id":31597,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Dragonborn (3.5)</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Max Stamina heightened by 1. Dexterity costs 1 more px, and cannot be more than 3 at character creation.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Size: </b>5</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Dragon defense:</b> +1 to Defense against dragons, Immune to dragon's frightful presence</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">+1 to Intimidate rolls.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Draconic Aspect:</b> Choose one between Heart, Mind and Wings.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>Heart:</i>Once per scene, a dragonborn can use the damaging breath weapon of the dragon species he belongs to. The dragonborn can roll Stamina + Ranged and use the successes as damage. All damage is bashing but becomes lethal at Arete 3. A cone shaped breath weapon is 5 meters long, while a line shaped is 9 meters.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>Mind:</i> The dragonborn is immune to sleep magic and paralisis. She gains darkvision 10 m, low light vision. At Arete 3 the dragonborn's darkvision is 20 meters, and he gains blindsense (see True Dragons).</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>Wings:</i> The dragonborn has wings. These wings are not yet able to let him fly, but are useful for jumping (+3 to jump), and allow the dragonborn to glide, negating falling damage. At Arete 3 the character can fly at its Speed.</span></span></li> </ol><ul><li><b>Languague:</b> Common, Draconic.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Dragonborn (4<sup>th</sup> edition)</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Max Stamina or Presence heightened by 1. Dexterity costs 1 more px, and cannot be more than 3 at character creation.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Size:</b> 5</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">+1 to Intimidate rolls</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Quick healer </b>merit.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Dragon breath: </b>a dragonborn can use the damaging breath weapon of the dragon species he belongs to. The dragonborn can roll Stamina + Ranged and use the successes as damage. All damage is bashing but becomes lethal at Arete 3. A cone shaped breath weapon is 5 meters long, while a line shaped is 9 meters.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Language:</b>Common, Draconic.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Thri-kreen</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Max Dexterity or Resolve heightened by 1. Manipulation costs 1 more px, and cannot be more than 3 at character creation.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Size:</b> 5</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Four Arms: </b>You have two extra arms. While you lack coordination to use them in combat, you can still use them to pick up items, like having two hands occupied and one with a torch. Once per turn you can sheathe/draw a weapon or retrieve/stow an item as a Reflexive action.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">+1 and 9 Again to all jumping rolls.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Chitin: </b>the thri-kreen has a starting Armor value of 1.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Natural weapons:</b> thri-kreen's bite and claws deal 0L. Bite can deliver a poison [Injection, Toxicity = Consitution, 1 bashing damage to Dexterity]</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Psychic Thri-kreen (</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>\u2022 or </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022\u2022</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Thri-kreen</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Thri-kreen are naturally psionics. These capabilities can be dispelled as any spell, because they are magical in nature.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">At the first dot, the thri-kreen is capable 3 times per day to use the following abilites:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>Chameleon:</i> Your skin camouflages with the surroundings. Roll Wits + Stealth. Every success adds to your next mundane Stealth dice pool or for the rest of the scene.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>Know direction:</i> roll Wits + Survival. You know where you in relation to important local or regional locations. You also know which direction you're facing.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">At two dots, the thri-kreen is capable once per day use the following abilities:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>Concealing amorpha:</i> you can replicate a <i>blur</i> spell rolling Wits + Subterfuge for the rest of the scene</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>Metaphysical claw:</i> Your claws and bite get a +1 to their damage for the rest of the scene.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T12:08:09-08:00","id":33335,"title":"","content":"Well the races I mentioned are the ones I was thinking of, I like the concept of warforged, shifters, half delkyr however they're called from eberron.<br /> <br /> Oh it occurred to me, you said this was a pathfinder game you converted, any chance of an adaption for the alchemist and summoner or do you want to just stick to the official 3x dnd?<br /> <br /> I find the summoner an intriguing concept, and I think a world that has both alchemists and artificers would probably get cyberpunk pretty fast. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 12-19-2013, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T13:59:04-08:00","id":33380,"title":"","content":"I'm not very familiar with alchemist and summoners, I don't really like their base concept. As for the summoner in particular, my worry is that a WoD conversion would be really too powerful, probably even more than the Pathfinder one. Summoning is already problematic in the base game, something I'm going to test in the next playtest is how a fighter can face a cleric with a summoned creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T14:51:47-08:00","id":33432,"title":"","content":"Added:<br /> All Spellcasting Merits for the new classes. Hexblade and Shugenja class rotes. Still missing: Spellthief, Warmage, Wu Jen rotes and Warlock invocations. That's going to be an awful lot of work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T17:26:16-08:00","id":34186,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Second playtest, Arete 2, 4 dots of magical items, +15 Experience. Fighter against Cleric.<br /> Arete 2, +15 Experience, 4 dots for magical items.<br /> <br /> <b>Red rain<br /> Class: </b>Fighter 2\u00b0 <b>Race:</b> Elf <b>Alignment:</b> Chaotic Good<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Intelligence 2 Wits 3 Resolve 2 Strenght 3 Dexterity 3 Stamina 3 Presence 2 Manipulation 2 Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Crafts 1, Occult (magic items) 3, Atlhetics 2, Weaponry (Sword) 3, Ranged (bow) 2, Empathy (Lies) 3, Intimidate 5, Subterfuge 2, Streetwise 1<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertize (Sword), Indomitable, Fleet of foot 3, Fast Reflexes 2, Defensive combat (Weaponry), Light Weapons 3 Quick draw (Weaponry), Resources 2<br /> <b>Skill Tricks:</b> Cripple, Don't mess with me<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9 <b>Defense:</b> 5 (6 without armor) <b>Armor: </b>3/1 (torso, arms) <b>Willpower: </b>5 <b>Initiative: </b>8 <b>Size: </b>5 <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Arete:</b> 2<br /> <b>Equipment:</b> Leather (heavy) +1, Sword +1, wand of <i>magic missile </i>(20 charges), potion of <i>aid</i>.<br /> <b>Attack:</b><br /> Sword +1, 3L , Initiative +8, 8 dice<br /> <b>Experience used</b> [Dexterity 3E, Wits 4E, Skill trick 2E, Light weapons 3E, Fast Reflexes 2E, Fleet of Foot 3]<br /> <br /> <b>Gollan Stonestorm</b><br /> <b>Class: </b>Cleric 2\u00b0 <b>Race: </b>Dwarf <b>Alignment:</b> Lawful evil<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Intelligence 1Wits 3 Resolve 4, Strenght 3 Dexterity 2 Stamina 6, Presence 2 Manipulation 2 Composure 2.<br /> <b>Skills: </b>Accademics (religion) 2,Occult (the Planes) 2<b>, </b>Survival 3Melee 3, Ranged (bow) 1Streetwise 3<b>, </b>Intimidate 3Persuasion 1 Subterfuge 4.<br /> <b>Merits: </b>Cleric 2, Hardy 1, Empower Spell, Professional Training (Religious, Accademics, Occult) 2, Quick draw (Ranged), Safe Place 2, Iron Stamina 3<br /> <b>Skill Tricks: </b>Quick Cram<br /> <b>Health: </b>12 <b>Defense: </b>3 (-2 for armor +3 for large shield) <b>Armor: </b>4/0 (torso, arms) <b>Willpower: </b>6 <b>Initiative:</b> 4 (2 with mace) <b>Size: </b>5 <b>Speed: </b>8<br /> <b>Arete: </b>2<br /> <b>Spells: </b><i>d</i><i>omains:</i> Strenght, Death. 6 per day<br /> 2<sup>nd </sup>level: Evil Eye, Stunning strenght, Summon Outsider<br /> 1<sup>st </sup>level: Bless<br /> <b>Equipment:</b> Chain mail +1, large shield +1, mace +2<br /> <b>Attack:</b><br /> Mace+2, 4L, 6 dice<br /> Bow (Strenght 3), 3L. 4 dice<br /> <b>Experience used:</b> [Stamina 12E, Iron Stamina 3E] Gollan Stonestorm, a dwarf cleric of a tyrannical deity of death and strenght, knows he's being hunted. He had the occasion to access a library and gain a Melee specialization in Mace, thanks to the Quick Cram Skill trick. Safe in an abandoned temple he uses as a Safe Place, he takes some candles, and uses some blood he obtained by hunting with Survival to create a magic circle. He starts to summon an imp hoping it will be quick. He needs 3 suxx, and the roll is penalized by the imp's Rank (1). His enemy will probably be here in an hour.<br /> Resolve 4 + Occult 2 +1 Special Level Bonus, -1 Rank is 6 dice. He uses a Willpower point to get 9 dice on the first roll and gets 3 suxx on the first try. The imp appears, summoned at the cleric's service. The imp expends 1 Essence to become invisibile. Power + Accuracy, exceptional suxx.<br /> Red rain is an elf fighter atoning for his sins against his deity. Having followed the steps of Gollan for many days, he used Resources to get a new <i>dispel magic </i>wand (Availability 1) to make sure he can dispel the cleric's spells in case he needed it, as he's very good at using magic items.<br /> He enters the temple, seeing Gollan, he starts glaring him, while around him the tension in the air becomes more tangible. Red rain is capable of making people shit their pants, and Gollan is no different, while he sweats.<br /> For the rest of the scene, Red Rain adds its Intimidate to his Defense up to when he recieved 3 points of damage or when he misses an attack roll. That means also the Imp, which while Red Rain can't see him, is still scared by the elf. Fortunately, Red Rain can't see him with only one success on his Perception roll, and he can attack him denying his Defense.<br /> The imp attacks Red Rain with its poisoned claws, using a Willpower attack. One success, 2 lethal damage, totally absorbed by Red Rain's Armor 3. That also fails to deliver any poison.<br /> Initiative time.<br /> Red Rain 15, Imp 13, Gollan 8.<br /> Red Rain quickly draws his magical sword and attacks the Imp, which could have shutted him down because of the dangerous poison (3 Dexterity bashing damage). He subtacts 3 to his Defense to get a +3 to the attack roll. 3 suxx, for a total 6 lethal damage against Corpus 3 and Armor 1. The Imp crashes on the floor, subdued by the damage.<br /> Gollan's turn. He reflexively casts Stunning Strenght, but rolls no successes. He approaches Red Rain and attacks him, using a Willpower point against Defense 7, 3 dice. 1 success, 5 lethal damage, absorbed by Armor 3. 2 Lethal for Red Rain. Not enough to break through Don' Mess With Me.<br /> New turn. Defense penalities are off for this turn, and Red Rain decides to take -5 to Defense to get +5 to Attack.<br /> Red Rains shouts at the dwarf, and swing his blade to the dwarf's left leg, taking -2 to the attack. 8 dice. Cripple Skill Trick will reduce the Dwarf's Speed to 1/10 (minimum Speed 1) until it gets medical attentions (which <i>cure light wounds</i> spells cannot cure).<br /> Three suxx, 6 lethal damage, Absorbed by Armor 4. For a total 2 damage to the dwarf. And then, uses his turn to move away from the dwarf.<br /> The dwarf cannot approach at a decent distance to the elf, so he casts Evil Eye on Red Rain. Resolve 4 + Occult 2 + SBL 1 \u2013 Red Rain's Composure 3, 4 dice. 2 suxx! -2 to the next active rolls for Red Rain!<br /> Red Rain has his new wand of <i>dispel magic</i> handy and uses it, reducing the Potency by 1. The dwarf drops the shield and takes out his bow to attack Red Rain, ignoring his Defense this way. Willpower, so it's 7 dice, ignoring Defense against ballistic Armor 1. 2 suxx, 4 total lethal damage! Now Red Rain has only 3 Health left.<br /> Red rain approaches the dwarf who now has no Defense because he dropped the shield to wield the bow, and attacks, leaving 5 to Defense (that means all of it) to get +5 to attack and using a Willpower, -1 for wound penality, -2 for the curse, -3 hitting to head. 4 successes, 7 lethal ignoring the Armor. Gollan is Stunned.<br /> Gollan's turn. He still has some Willpower, which he uses to end the Stunned Tilt, taking -3 to all actions for that turn. He still has his mace, which was hanged to his hand thanks to its lace, while shooting.<br /> Time to use Stunning Strenght, hoping he can hit and stun Red Rain. Luckily he does not suffer any wound penality thanks to Iron Stamina 3. 1 success! That's enough to empower his strike, should he hit.<br /> While his Defense is 0, it's because he's penalyzed by the armor, not because he's helpless, so he can still get an all-out attack.<br /> Strenght 3 + Melee 3 + Specialization 1 + All out attack 2, -3 for the Stunned Tilt, against Defense 0.<br /> 1 lethal damage! His mace hits Red Rain, who must now roll Stamina to avoid being Stunned.<br /> Red Rain cannot use Willpower because he already used it in this turn. Luckily he has Arete 2, which gives him a +1 to this roll. 4 dice. Too bad for Gollan, it's 3 successes to save.<br /> Red Rain now has 2 Health, -2 wound penality. It's now or never. Lose 5 to Defense to gain 5 to attack. Willpower. 8 dice + 5 Light Weapons + 3 Willpower \u2013 2 wound penality it's 14 dice against no Defense. 4 successes. Armor soaks 4 damage, but Gollan finally falls on the ground helpless and bleeding out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Comments:</b>Ok, the fighter was astoundingly powerful while not being maxed on melee and strenght. The second dot of light weapons is really powerful and perhaps a little too much in a world where attack bonuses are rare and Defense is generally higher because of Athletics. The fighter used little Willpower too.<br /> Anyway the fighter had been really lucky and seriously risked to be killed. If the cleric succeded in stunning the fighter with Stunning Strenght, things might have gone a little different. The imp was also really unlucky. The imp could have taken him to Dexterity 0 and the encounter would have ended there. Probably if Gollan managed summoned a kyton or a barbazu instead of an imp, he could have killed the Red Rain easily.<br /> ...Well, unless Red Rain took care of them using the Cripple Skill Trick on them to lock them down and then switch to kill the cleric. Which could have been possibile.<br /> <br /> Sooo...Level 2, an optimized fighter might take care of summons and eventually kill a melee spellcaster with a bit of luck. Yay.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T10:57:00-07:00","id":93584,"title":"","content":"Sorry people for not posting anything. Just know that I'm updating the core book right now, and writing it in Italian for my group and my italian friends.<br /> <br /> Dungeons &amp; Darkness has been through a lot of changes while I wasn't posting here.<br /> <br /> Various fixes on the classes, new spells, new merits, cleaned up mechanics, overhauled and more balanced monsters, diminished the needed books to play with (thanks to making some rules optional) and new magic items.<br /> The book is not finished yet, but when it is, I WILL definitely translate it in English to allow you to play the game with the new features. Unfortunately I'm alone in this work, so I'm not that fast. Right now I just finished the spell lists for the core classes, except for Cleric Domains.<br /> I'd like to develop epic levels, psionics, rules for deities and things like that, but I'm really busy completing the main book and having a solid base on which I can write.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T02:45:54-07:00","id":136459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I started translating the updated book in English yesterday night. Many changes, even from the start. I hope this version is being clearer, with less typos and less obvious errors. Leave a comment if you wish here or on the document if you wish so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T22:11:24-07:00","id":137711,"title":"","content":"Okay I'll take look and see what jumps out at me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T17:37:46-07:00","id":138670,"title":"","content":"Classes completed, Alignment rules completed.<br /> Still to do<ul><li>Merits</li> <li>Magic rules</li> <li>Magic items</li> <li>Special materials</li> <li>Planes</li> <li>Spell lists</li> <li>Monsters</li> <li>Prestige classes</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T04:42:02-07:00","id":140419,"title":"","content":"Which is funny, because I remember the document having rules for those lol. <br /> <br /> Nothing struck me from a quick look through on the stuff you've got so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T07:17:22-07:00","id":140480,"title":"","content":"The original document did, this one is a re-make. All the rules that changed need to be re-written, all that were ok can stay. I'll eliminate all references from Mage the Awakening and Werewolf the Forsaken on the spells to make consultation easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T02:40:38-07:00","id":149265,"title":"","content":"First chapter done. DONE DONE DONE DONE. Yay. Now to <b>Chapter 2</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit </a> </div> <d