/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ychIYHpWoHFUp2DoUEWHKiJd6gJbvWKhb-iecc0Q9CE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ychIYHpWoHFUp2DoUEWHKiJd6gJbvWKhb-iecc0Q9CE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ychIYHpWoHFUp2DoUEWHKiJd6gJbvWKhb-iecc0Q9CE/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Prestige classes completed! Loaded in both the main document and the link above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T08:40:45-07:00","id":227054,"title":"","content":"Hi there!<br /> Is anyone willing to help me?<br /> I need someone to give me feedback on the system and someone helping with actual developing would also be much appreciated.<br /> I know some things might be improved, the game is incomplete as it stands now. But doing all the job alone is tiring, and I already work on it almost three days per week.<br /> <br /> Is anyone availabile?<br /> <br /> When the Corebook is completed enough, I might even ST a play by chat or play by Hangouts cronicle to do some more extensive playtest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T23:09:45-07:00","id":235076,"title":"","content":"You have some very compelling stuff. So far I'm liking it. I'm currently &quot;playtesting&quot; it in my chronicle as we speak by introducing antagonists and allied NPCs who use these rules as we go along. I don't have anything concrete yet as I just came across this a couple of weeks ago.<br /> <br /> What exactly do you want as far as feedback? Do you have any specific questions or more just general feedback?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T09:44:12-07:00","id":235496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiarn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/2493-dungeon-darkness?p=235076#post235076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have some very compelling stuff. So far I'm liking it. I'm currently &quot;playtesting&quot; it in my chronicle as we speak by introducing antagonists and allied NPCs who use these rules as we go along. I don't have anything concrete yet as I just came across this a couple of weeks ago.<br /> <br /> What exactly do you want as far as feedback? Do you have any specific questions or more just general feedback?</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of setting are you playing? Standard world of darkness (lol)? Fantasy? Other?<br /> <br /> EDIT: IF fantasy, homemade or existing D&amp;D setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T03:17:45-07:00","id":236311,"title":"","content":"It's a fantasy setting. Not an existing setting but a somewhat typical D&amp;D setting (most countries are medieval with a feudal society). There are, of course, exceptions. But overall it tends to be a very typical &quot;delve into a forgotten tomb full of traps one minute then negotiate a trade treaty with rival lords the next&quot; D&amp;D type game.<br /> The PCs, however, are mostly normal WoD characters (a vampire, a promethean, a geist and a dark hero (from mirrors) to be exact) because we started a while before I found this thread and started reading it. That's why it's becoming a mix through NPCs to see how the two interact.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I don't even know how you'd run a standard WoD setting with these type of characters lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T09:44:58-07:00","id":236591,"title":"","content":"Well, D&amp;Darkness wasn't originally meant to work with actual WoD splats, so for now I need to know how they compare. And I'd also needed to know how balanced are classes.<br /> <br /> You could theoretically give your character class levels if they wished so, using their Supernatural Tolerance (Blood Potency, Azoth and so on) as Arete and allow them to spend 2 Experiences to buy a level (that's what I do for &quot;classed&quot; dragons and outsiders), up to their Supernatural Tolerance.<br /> <br /> For the rest, if anything &quot;wrong&quot; comes up, or anything unclear, please contact me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T00:03:54-07:00","id":241145,"title":"","content":"Ok, here are some things you need to know about what I've been using and what I haven't (obviously I have no feedback for the stuff I haven't used yet) before we begin.<br /> I have been using the classes, and skill tricks as you suggested.<br /> I've used your merits <i>except</i> for any item creation ones. I do something different for that.<br /> <br /> I have not touched or even looked at race, since I use a different variant for that in my chronicle.<br /> I have not used alignment at all, nor even read that section.<br /> <br /> All-in-all when comparing them to a typical splat (vampire, changeling, etc) the big thing I've noticed is spellcaster-specific. When you are a vampire and you want to use a power, you spend blood. Then you go eat, so you get some blood back. Then you have full blood. (Simplified, I know, but it's the <i>point</i> I'm trying to make here.) When you are, say, a wizard, you cast your spells. Then you wait until tomorrow. I think the spellcasters could do with some way of getting their &quot;mana/spellslots/what-have-you&quot; back that wasn't just &quot;go to sleep.&quot; World of Darkness as a whole tends to avoid the &quot;per day&quot; thing and I think it's a point in their favor for it. Each class could even be different if you wanted (I.E. Bards have to socialize, similar to a changeling gleaning glamour, Wizards study, Clerics pray, Druids tromp around in the woods, etc). I know my players often take breaks in the middle of whatever they are doing to feed/whatever and come back at an issue at full strength. These classes would just have to wait until tomorrow.<br /> <br /> I've also noticed that the &quot;template&quot; as a whole is a little underwhelming when compared to the other splats. (Maybe the racial stuff would fix this, I will take a look at that.) One of the things I've always noticed about the Dark Hero from Mirrors is that it's missing a lot of &quot;cool things&quot; that simply <i>being</i> one of the other things gives you. (for example: a vampire doesn't breath, so gas effects won't work on them. Most poisons don't affect vampires or mummies. Prometheans can eat almost anything and go for days without sleep, etc) It's a lot of little things I guess, but if you are intending to be &quot;dungeon delving&quot; and more &quot;heroic fantasy&quot; in your chronicle, it's certainly stuff that has great advantage.<br /> <br /> Now, onto the classes.<br /> As a whole, most of the spellcasters are pretty useful, cool. They are things I would try out (and have, as NPCs for some of them.) So I don't have a problem with your spellcasting system overall aside from the energy recharging I mentioned above. I will list out the individual class in order and my thoughts/suggestions on them.<br /> <u>Bard</u>: This one has strong flavor and overall works well. A couple of notes/questions though. If a bard has to maintain concentration (which implies she needs to keep singing) to <i>fascinate</i> how does she talk to people to benefit from the +2 to presence rolls when talking to people? <i>Inspire competence</i> is a little underwhelming. I have to use one of my uses of music for the day to give an ally a +1 to something? Why don't I just teamwork instead and give her my successes? Chances are, even untrained, I'm going to give her a +1 <i>without</i> resorting to magic.<br /> <br /> <u>Sorcerer</u>: I've only had one so far and only at the second level. But so far worked great.<br /> <br /> <u>Wizard:</u> This is probably more of an issue with your item creation merits than <i>scribe scroll</i> but we're talking about the wizard here so I'm bringing it up. Perhaps this was your intention but Willpower is easy to get back. &quot;Spell slots&quot; come back every day. The extended action to make a scroll doesn't take that much time/effort/successes. Do you realize that an average wizard can churn out whatever spellslots they have in scrolls <i>each day</i> fairly easily? Give a wizard a week in a city and they will literally run out of carrying capacity before they run out of spells or even need to take a break to replenish.<br /> <br /> <u>Barbarian<b>: </b></u>I only just introduced a barb antagonist but so far this class is looking fine.<br /> <br /> <u>Fighter:</u> Here is where the criticism comes in. This class is just worthless. At the higher levels it has some interesting things which I think should stay but it definitely needs more. For example, at the first level, literally the <i>only</i> thing you get from this class is the ability to change your weapon specialization (which you do at least, get for free) So I'm getting something that would cost me 1 experience and the ability to change that into a different one? And I would prefer this to spells? or raging? or sneak attack? The answer is no, no one would ever take this at first level. It needs more. And 2nd level isn't any better. You get bonus initiative (a merit) but only when using a specified weapon? That's boring and underpowered. Third level improves a bit, but it's confusing. I spend an action to lower an opponents defense (for everyone? or just me?) for the scene. I assume by only one since the next line tells me I can spend multiple turns to lower it more, up to my fighter level. That ability is useful, and also flavorful. You read their body language to counter their fighting style. Yes. Then we get back to ho-hum and nigh-useless. A dice bonus to things Brawl covers? Seriously? All this weapons stuff up to now and then we make them brawl better? What about letting me use my weaponry (with my specialized weapon, of course) <i>instead</i> of brawl, to grapple, trip, or whatever. And the culmination being to lower my target number is pretty neat, but this should not be the pivotal ability, that thing I've striven for my entire fighting career. This needs to be like the second level ability. It's not powerful enough as the ultimate ability when the wizard up there is throwing around chain lightnings. And why doesn't the fighter (as one of the few classes that uses it extensively) get any armor abilities? Like lesser speed penalties, or better armor bonus because they wear it better. Something like that? Overall the fighter needs a lot of help.<br /> <br /> <u>Monk<br /> Paladin<br /> Priest<br /> Druid</u><br /> So far haven't fit these in just yet.<br /> <br /> <u>Ranger</u> So far so good. Don't have one above the third level yet but everything seems to be working well so far. Though their <i>woodland stride</i> ability would be better if there were more things in WoD that used this. I've only seen about two tilts. So perhaps add more &quot;terrain tilts&quot;? I know I'd love to see some terrain stuff.<br /> <br /> <u>Rogue:</u> I like the rogue so far. Though I allow the <i>danger sense</i> merit to apply to traps automatically (and give the bonus when she's actively searching for them as well). I think you should really just rewrite it to a +2 bonus to notice hidden enemies and find traps/secret doors (and of course giving her 9-again on the traps from her trapfinding). Sneak attack is a little underwhelming so far. I might rework it to be like <i>powerful success</i> from the Dark Heroes and let you know how that goes. I don't know yet. (Also, for the sneak attack, if a person is hidden and attacks from surprise, they <i>already</i> get rote quality on the attack. So technically all your sneak attack does is give bonus dice on attacks when &quot;flanking&quot;.) And you might want to include things that sneak attacks works/doesn't work on. Depending on the edition in D&amp;D it didn't work on undead, constructs, plants, etc. In your system it works on everything. An fyi.<br /> <br /> <u>Merits:</u> So far, from the ones I've looked at/used, I'm pleased. I do think, however, you could use some more class specific ones for some classes. For instance the Barbarian, Fighter, and Rogue, don't have <i>any</i>. For the Fighter and Barbarian, fighting style merits could really step up their game. And a rogue should <i>shine</i> with merits. They are, after all, the skill-heavy class in D&amp;D. They should have so many tricks.<br /> <br /> That's what I have so far. Hope it helps, and I'll keep you posted as more becomes available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T13:01:34-07:00","id":241629,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">What do you think of this change on the fighter and the Merits? Any suggestion or substition?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Fighter</b></span></span></span> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Experts in the techniques of fighting, they can be soldiers, men and womens at arms, noble warriors or trained rebellious.</span></span></span> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Class Skills: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Archery, Athletics, Brawl, Crafts, Weaponry</span></span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Weapon aptitude, Weapon specialization, Fighter\u2019s measure</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022\u2022</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Uncanny initiative, Armed Expertise</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Study enemy</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Maneuver expertize</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Visage of threat</span></span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Weapon aptitude:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> If a fighter can take some time with an adequate weapon (or his body) for at least ten minutes of a quiet place, he can switch a Specialization (and any related Area of Specialization) in Archery, Athletics, Brawl or Weaponry related to a weapon (or his unarmed attack) to the weapon he wants to master at the moment. This change lasts for the rest of the story or when the fighter decides to use this class feature again.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Weapon specialization: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">A fighter gains a free Specialization in any weapon of his choice, or takes the Area of Specialization in said Specialization if present.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Fighter\u2019s measure: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Once per session, a fighter can make a guess on an enemy, trying to determine who is the strongest.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dice pool:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Wits + Level - Composure</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dramatic failure:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The fighter jumps to wrong conclusions.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Failure: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">The fighter can\u2019t read the opponent.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Success:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The fighter understands whether the enemy is less, more or equally powerful, and to which lenght. Note that this class feature only determines powerfulness in \u201ccombat\u201d. An expert assassin might not sound as stronger than him, but he might be much more powerful when he can choose the moment of the attack.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Exceptional success:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The fighter gains the Steadfast Condition.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Uncanny initiative:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> At 2</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">nd</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> level, the fighter gains an Initiative bonus equal to his fighter level when he uses a weapon which he as a Specialization for. This includes Specializations acquired through Weapon aptitude.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Armed expertize: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">At 2</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">nd</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> level,by spending 1 Willpower point, the fighter can reduce the target number of his attack rolls to 7 instead of 8. That means he can get successes with a result of 7.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Study enemy.</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> At 3</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">rd</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> level, the fighter can study an opponent for a turn to lower its Defense by one against the fighter for the rest of the scene. The fighter can take more turns to lower this value up to his fighter level in Defense. The fighter must be able to see the opponent. This class feature can occur prior the start of a combat, if the fighter can take time to study the opponent.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Maneuver expertize</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: At 4</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">th</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> level, the fighter can spend 1 Willpower to add half his Level (round up) to all contested rolls to grapple, trip, disarm and knock him back for the entire scene.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Visage of threat:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> At 5</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">th</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> level, when the fighter is in combat, he looks immediately more threatening to those who oppose him. All enemies facing the character suffer -4 to their Initiative modifier as they flinch back from his presence.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>CLASS EXCLUSIVE MERITS</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Warrior\u2019s Insight (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Prerequisite: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Fighter 3, Wits 3, War 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Benefit: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">The character can use Fighter\u2019s measure once per scene instead of once per story. If the character attains success in this roll while studying that enemy with the fighter\u2019s class feature, the character he will subtract -2 instead of -1 to his opponent\u2019s Defense (up to his Level as normal). The fighter can use Fighter\u2019s measure on enemies he already studied to gain the benefit of studying, exactly as written above. For example, if the character takes a turn to study the enemy and uses Fighter\u2019s measure successfully in the same turn, the Defense penalty would be -2 instead of -1.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Quick study (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Prerequisite: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Fighter 4, War 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Benefit: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">The character using Study enemy can roll Wits + War - the highest Composure to apply Study enemy to all opponents he can see. A failed roll will apply Study enemy only to a single opponent.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Pre-emptive counter (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Prerequisite: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Fighter 3, War 5, Weaponry or Brawl 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Benefit: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">If the character has used Study enemy at least one turn on the enemy and be ready to attack with a Brawl or Weaponry attack, the character can attempt a \u201ccounter attack\u201d. The enemy must be within reach of the weapon. The fighter uses the attack to subtract successes on the attack of the opponent.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 08-26-2014, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T23:00:00-07:00","id":242029,"title":"","content":"Also notice that: No, surprise attacks don't get the rote action by default, if that's what you wanted to point out. Surprise attacks only leave the target without Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T11:36:54-07:00","id":261373,"title":"","content":"I don't know if anyone noticed, but I upgraded classes and the magic system. I added some merits for about every class, and cleaned up class features.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T02:11:56-07:00","id":271491,"title":"","content":"Rules for alchemy and alchemical items added in the Skill Modification section of the first chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T01:49:58-07:00","id":279457,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Yay, Demons and Devils completed!</b><br /> <br /> <b>Important changes</b>: demons and devils no longer have a &quot;random number, random creature&quot; summon devil/demon, and now there are fixed and somewhat clearer rules on how to give a demon the ability to summon something. Like for Celestials, they use Skills, have Attribute cap 5 and have a minimum quantity of Merits. All properties of devils and demons have been compiled in an easy to use reference block taken from the ephemeral entity creation, to have a lower page count and lower wall of text. Short description for each fiend is present like I did for celestials.<br /> I hope this way <i>Summon monster</i> and <i>Summon greater outsiders </i>won't be so powerful like it was earlier, against entities with 15 dice or more to attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Still to do:</b><br /> Aberrations (Aboleth, chaos beast, ettercap, intellect devourer, naga)<br /> Common races and Trolls/Giants/Ogres (Hill giant, hobgoblin, kobold, ogre, ogremage, orc, storm giant, tiefling, troll)<br /> Dragons (I'll have to tweak base stats because Occult is no longer the main Skill for casting)<br /> Fey (kitsune, nymph, satyr, pixie, treant)<br /> Undead<br /> Werewolves<br /> Half celestials, half dragons, half-fiends</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T16:50:30-08:00","id":337526,"title":"","content":"Hey, Jesun!<br /> <br /> Wanted to let you know I'm using your work as a base to run a Warcraft game (Warcraft: the Conflict). So far, your system is great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T17:01:14-08:00","id":337534,"title":"","content":"Oh thank you, thank you very much for your feedback!<br /> Do you feel like anything in particular could be better?<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Are you using Occult or all the skills for spellcasting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T19:09:30-08:00","id":337629,"title":"","content":"I'm using different skills depending on the spell. One of the thing's I've done is gone back and given all the classes a Fuel Stat, Arcane classes (mages, warlocks, necromancers) use Mana, Spiritual classes (Priests, paladins, shamans, druids, monks and rangers) use Essence, and Martial classes use Conviction (like a small extra pool of Willpower). I feel that this helps balance casters and non-casters, while also keeping the 5-minute workday problem be non-existent. As for the skills, I use all of them. It's not... mm, based on Spell School (since those are kind of guidelines) but based on it's effect, and which class it's on a list. It makes it a pain to do all the dicepools, and so far, I've just told each player what it is when asked, based on their class.<br /> <br /> If you're interested here's what I have; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fnfoMaLf99zfH0pAaqJiEeVVB7RUHlfT1bbN7YYHPDo/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...bN7YYHPDo/edit</a><br /> <br /> So far, everything is based on what my players are using. I'll fill out other things as I go along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 12-12-2014, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T01:20:43-08:00","id":337878,"title":"","content":"Hey, really cool!<br /> You modified this system pretty heavily, but for Warcraft, that's excellent. Congrats!<br /> I'm not entirely sure of what Conviction does...are you going to give fighter and rogue special maneuvers or something like that?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Really, you did an amazing job!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 12-12-2014, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T18:34:52-08:00","id":338597,"title":"","content":"Yes! A lot of Martial classes' Class Merits will use Conviction, and it can be spent to power Skill Tricks. It's like an extra pool of Willpower, and lets them spend multiple willpower per turn. I'm also looking to use it as a way to interact with the system, above and beyond spending Willpower to do things. So, like Skill Tricks that require Conviction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T02:02:37-08:00","id":338906,"title":"","content":"Fey almost ready. I expanded them to a little more, with annis, sea hag and green hag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T11:12:19-08:00","id":339233,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Fey added!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Annis, Darkling, Green Hag, Kitsune, Nymph, Pixie, Satyr, Sea Hag, Treant and Elder Treant, Unicorn!</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T17:52:01-08:00","id":339593,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Yaaay, <b>Other common races</b> completed!</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Common races (Aasimar, Cloud giant, Drow, Fire giant, Frost Giant, Goblin, Hill giant, Hobgoblin, Kobold, Ogre, Ogre magi, Orc, Storm giant, Trolls, Tiefling)</span></span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T01:24:41-08:00","id":395962,"title":"","content":"Ok, I couldn't resist to make a new overhaul of spells. Unfortunately I'm a perfectionist (though this overhaul is far from perfect) I added some more classical spells from the PHB and removed some spells that were uncharacteristic.<br /> <br /> Potency is now not tied to damage anymore, and most spells do not do more damage with successes. Damage can still be upgraded with Empowered Spell, as well as healing spells. But you have to get penalties to cast a pumped up spell.<br /> Now you don't pull of a fireball with 10 lethal damage because you rolled 4 successes, used Spell power to increase the Potency, and Empowered spell to get a -10 to get a +5 to Potency.<br /> A standard <i>fireball</i> does 3 bashing fire damage, which can become 7 bashing with an empowered -10 spell.<br /> <br /> <b>Still to do:</b><br /> Aberration<br /> Dragons (they're on the way)<br /> Undead (they're on the way)<br /> Werewolves.<br /> Condition summary.<br /> Guidelines for 1e play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit?pli=1</pre> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 02-07-2015, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T15:18:51-08:00","id":396818,"title":"","content":"Have you considered mining <a href=\"http://lawfulnice.blogspot.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Dungeons: The Dragoning</i></a> for ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T16:25:39-08:00","id":396897,"title":"","content":"Dungeon the Dragoning is a really different game with totally different premises. And a totally different game system. I gave it a watch, but I didn't find anything useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T08:54:37-08:00","id":403358,"title":"","content":"Dragons are up!<br /> <br /> <b>Still to do:</b><br /> Aberration<br /> Undead (they're on the way)<br /> Werewolves.<br /> Condition summary.<br /> Guidelines for 1e play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T14:40:27-08:00","id":403727,"title":"","content":"Undead added to the monsters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T13:43:37-08:00","id":409278,"title":"","content":"I like how you have done this. I might borrow your document for typing out my own rules. For my races, I adjusted the minimum and maximums of races, and gave each race a unique merit chain. Half-Elves, Half-Orcs and other Half-Humans use the human merit chain, but have the racial adjustments of their non-human parent.<br /> For classes, I borrowed abilities from Mage Legacies, and reworded them to run off willpower, auto-activate, with successess equal to class dots (1-5, same xp cost as gnosis, abilities gained at 1, 3, 5). This way, classes are secondary less than tertiary to characters, and not affected by outside influences. It helps with balance, and to maintain focus on who the character is, and not what class they are. Using Witchfinder's Gutter Magic for general spellcasting, which anyone can learn.<br /> <br /> Edit: My alignment is also subjective. Each player has to provide examples of what they consider actions appropriate to each alignment, graded for severity. It really makes Paladin's interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4981-skaeren","name":"skaeren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T14:17:51-07:00","id":562221,"title":"","content":"Hi people!<br /> It's been some time since I last posted, I'm sorry. I've been busy with &quot;life&quot;, but the 1.2 version of <b>Dungeons &amp; Darkness</b> is complete! Theoretically what's missing is the appendix for 1e games, but I'm not really sure anyone would care to play it in 1e anyway. <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>All rights reserved to their rightful owners, this is a fan work and is meant as an admiration for both World of Darkness and Dungeons &amp; Dragons (and Pathfinder RPG to a degree). Any text for existing Conditions and Tilt or other material printed in other books is written only for ease of use.</b></span></span></span> <br /> <b>Dungeons &amp; Darkness</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit?pli=1</pre> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iryDzCFWDg7xyTwZ9egnWLCpIgYiVMJ6T7SHbjzkynE/edit?pli=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> At the moment, I'm working on the expansion, with psionics and the classes from the Complete books, as well as epic level material! Stay tuned!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T03:14:47-08:00","id":1165001,"title":"","content":"This might be a bit of a necropost, but this is such amazing work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4981-skaeren","name":"skaeren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}